          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What does guidance describe about starting a statin, and which risk bands are used?",
          "answer": "The search results did not answer your question. None of the passages describe when to start a statin or which risk bands are used. The results listed a document called \"guideline-lipid-screening-and-statin-initiation\" as a source, but no text from it appeared.\n\nThe results did include other material:\n\n- **Coronary artery disease secondary prevention** (guideline-coronary-artery-disease-secondary-prevention) covers treatments after a heart attack, including blood-pressure targets and cardiac rehabilitation. It does not describe statin starting criteria.\n- **Hypertension: when treatment starts and which options are first-line** (guideline-hypertension-first-line-treatment) uses an estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk of 10 percent or higher as one trigger for drug treatment. This applies to blood-pressure treatment, not statins, so it should not be read as a statin rule.\n- **Type 2 diabetes: first-line pharmacologic management** (guideline-type-2-diabetes-first-line-therapy) and **Type 2 diabetes: who is screened, and the diagnostic thresholds** (guideline-type-2-diabetes-screening) cover diabetes medicines and screening. Neither addresses statins.\n\nYou could try a narrower search, such as \"lipid screening and statin initiation criteria.\" You could also ask a clinician or pharmacist, who can explain how cardiovascular risk is assessed for you and whether a statin is worth discussing.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
